1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,718
A three-tonne dragon is ten times

2
00:00:01,718 --> 00:00:03,100
heavier than the biggest animal that

3
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:03,912
ever flew.

4
00:00:04,249 --> 00:00:05,364
It can flap all day and

5
00:00:05,364 --> 00:00:06,524
never leave the ground.

6
00:00:06,861 --> 00:00:08,580
So you make your bones hollow,

7
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:09,566
like a bird's.

8
00:00:09,776 --> 00:00:11,493
Your whole skeleton gets lighter.

9
00:00:11,923 --> 00:00:13,501
But hollow bones snap.

10
00:00:13,769 --> 00:00:15,151
One hard landing and your wing

11
00:00:15,151 --> 00:00:15,823
breaks.

12
00:00:16,335 --> 00:00:17,752
So you brace them inside with

13
00:00:17,752 --> 00:00:18,935
tiny struts,

14
00:00:18,982 --> 00:00:20,572
like a vulture's wing bones.

15
00:00:21,002 --> 00:00:22,221
Light as a straw,

16
00:00:22,221 --> 00:00:23,451
strong as a bridge.

17
00:00:23,882 --> 00:00:25,112
But you're still far too heavy

18
00:00:25,112 --> 00:00:26,214
to flap your way up.

19
00:00:26,645 --> 00:00:27,724
So you don't flap.

20
00:00:27,887 --> 00:00:28,944
You climb to the top of

21
00:00:28,944 --> 00:00:29,570
a volcano,

22
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:30,452
and you jump.

23
00:00:30,615 --> 00:00:32,460
But gliding only goes one way:

24
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:33,250
down.

25
00:00:33,518 --> 00:00:34,724
So you ride the heat.

26
00:00:34,841 --> 00:00:36,536
Hot air rising off the volcano

27
00:00:36,536 --> 00:00:37,488
lifts you in circles,

28
00:00:37,488 --> 00:00:39,149
like a condor that can soar

29
00:00:39,149 --> 00:00:40,612
for five hours without a single

30
00:00:40,612 --> 00:00:41,215
flap.

31
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:44,082
That's why dragons live on volcanoes.

32
00:00:44,246 --> 00:00:45,243
Not for the fire.

33
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:46,451
For the lift.

